Students were asked to report information regarding their workload. This includes work from both paid/unpaid jobs, academic work, as well as time spent caregiving for any family members.

*See [Information on Missing Data](index.qmd#md)*

## Weekly Paid Work Hours




::: {.cell layout-align="center"}
::: {.cell-output-display}
![Figure 3.1. Weekly Paid Work Hours (n=49, 98% of 50 reporting).](Workload_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-2-1.png){fig-align='center' width=576}
:::
:::




**Survey Question:** *Estimate the number of hours you work in a PAID job (e.g. server at a restaurant, office assistant, etc.) or paid internship (e.g. training, shadowing, or practicum) per week.*

**Summary:** Students reported a wide range of paid work hours per week with an average of 16.61 hours (denoted by the dotted line) and a median of 20. The majority of students worked either part-time or not at all. Only 5 (10.2%) students were considered to be working full-time (40 or more hours per week).


<br>

## Impact of COVID




::: {.cell layout-align="center"}
::: {.cell-output-display}
![Figure 3.2. Impact of COVID (n=45, 90% of 50 reporting).](Workload_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-3-1.png){fig-align='center' width=768}
:::
:::





**Survey Question:** *Have the hours you work in a PAID job or internship changed due to COVID-19?*

**Summary:** A total of 7 (15.6%) students reported not working prior to COVID, while 11 (24.4%) reported that their hours have not changed due to COVID. There were 11 (24.4%) students that had their hours decreased, 11 (24.4%) that no longer had a job/internship, and 5 (11.1%) that had their hours increased. 


<br>

## Unpaid Work Hours




::: {.cell layout-align="center"}
::: {.cell-output-display}
![Figure 3.3. Unpaid Work Hours (n=45, 90% of 50 reporting).](Workload_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-4-1.png){fig-align='center' width=576}
:::
:::




**Survey Question:** *Estimate the number of hours you work in an UNPAID internship (e.g. training, shadowing, practicum, and/or volunteer, etc.) per week. Do not combine with answers above.*

**Summary:** The average number of unpaid work hours was 7 (denoted by the dotted line) and the median was 0. A total of 23 (51.1%) students did not work at an unpaid job/internship, while 16 (35.6%) students reported working 10 or more unpaid hours every week. 

<br>



## Unpaid Caregiving Hours




::: {.cell layout-align="center"}
::: {.cell-output-display}
![Figure 3.4. Unpaid Caregiving Hours (n=45, 90% of 50 reporting).](Workload_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-5-1.png){fig-align='center' width=576}
:::
:::




**Survey Question:** *Estimate the number of hours you spend each week on UNPAID family obligations (e.g. taking care of younger siblings, preparing family meals, running errands for the family, etc.) per week.*

**Summary:** A total of 35 (77.8%) students spent time each week caring for family members with an average of 16.31 hours (denoted by the dotted line) and a median of 10. There were 10 (22.2%) students that reported spending zero hours per week on family obligations, while 5 (11.1%) reported spending 40 or more hours each week. 


<br>

## Academic Workload




::: {.cell layout-align="center"}
::: {.cell-output-display}
![Figure 3.5. Academic Workload (n=50, 100% of 50 reporting).](Workload_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-6-1.png){fig-align='center' width=576}
:::
:::




**Survey Question:** *How many units are you currently taking?*

**Additional Notes:** The hours of academic work per week were estimated by assuming 3 hours of work per unit. 

**Summary:** The average number of academic hours worked per week was 42.2 hours (denoted by the dotted line), while the median was 45. A total of 28 (56.0%) students spent 40 or more hours per week on academic work.

<br />

## Non-Academic Workload




::: {.cell layout-align="center"}
::: {.cell-output-display}
![Figure 3.6. Non-Academic Workload (n=45, 90% of 50 reporting).](Workload_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-7-1.png){fig-align='center' width=576}
:::
:::




**Survey Question:** *This variable was derived by taking the sum of students' paid work hours, unpaid work hours, and caregiving hours.*

**Additional Notes:** Non-academic workload was calculated only for students who reported their paid work hours, unpaid work hours, and caregiving hours. 


**Summary:** The average total number of hours worked per week in non-academic matters was 38.91 hours (denoted by the dotted line), while the median was 36 hours. A total of 19 (42.2%) students spent 40 or more hours per week on non-academic work. 


<br />

## Total Workload




::: {.cell layout-align="center"}

:::

::: {.cell layout-align="center"}
::: {.cell-output-display}
![Figure 3.7. Total Workload (n=45, 90% of 50 reporting).](Workload_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-9-1.png){fig-align='center' width=576}
:::
:::




**Survey Question:** *This variable was derived by taking the sum of students' paid work hours, unpaid work hours, caregiving hours, and hours spent from academic activities (assuming 3 hours per unit taken).*


**Additional Notes:** Total workload was calculated only for students who reported their paid work hours, unpaid work hours, caregiving hours, and units. 


**Summary:** The average number of total hours worked per week was 79.58 hours (denoted by the dotted line), while the median was 77 hours. A total of 44 (97.8%) students spent 40 or more hours per week on academic and non-academic work, while 20 (44.4%) spent 80 or more hours. 





